#! `documentSymbol` nesting is behavior, not presentation: the outline is
#! compared as a multiset at the top level (LSP fixes no order) with every
#! element `exact`, so a struct that stops containing its fields, or a symbol
#! whose selectionRange stops being inside its range, turns this red.
#! `errors.lu` carries structs, functions, and `!T` error rows at three
#! depths.
name      requests/document-symbol
profile   minimal

initialize
open      errors.lu
wait      diagnostics errors.lu
req       documentSymbol errors.lu
shutdown
